# rail_simulation stack

- Vite + Vue 3 (`<script setup>`) + TypeScript + Tailwind v4 + Rust compiled with `wasm-pack`
- Vue is the delivery layer: params, playback, status text, routing, theme
- Domain and simulation steps live in `wasm/` (Rust). Do not reimplement them in Vue
- WASM layers: `domain/` (pure state), `render/` (colors + GraphicsEngine), `adapters/` (wasm_bindgen), `canvas_graphics_engine.rs` (Canvas only)
- Draw through `GraphicsEngine`; do not add Canvas 2D calls inside domain or adapters beyond constructing the engine
- Theme tokens (`brand`, `surface-*`, `content-*`) for UI chrome. Algorithm pointer colors may stay explicit
- Pages go in `src/pages/`, composables in `src/composables/`, routes in `src/router/`
- Add a simulation as a WASM type + a Vue page + a router entry. Do not create a new app shell

## Ignore from catalog rules unless the user asks

Pinia, Nuxt, DaisyUI, shadcn/ui, VueUse, Solana/Anchor, Next.js
